1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Christopher Andreas Lange III, born in Stavanger on 10 November 1818, graduated 
2 CONT
2 CONT in Stavanger in 1836 and received the mark "laud", graduated in theology 1843 and 
2 CONT
2 CONT received a passing grade. He first worked as a house teacher for minister Heidenreich in 
2 CONT
2 CONT Askim, later for district attorney Fougner at Ringerike and thereafter as a private teacher 
2 CONT
2 CONT in Kongsvinger until 1852 when he became manager of the school for citizens of Brevik. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 13 August 1857 he was named personal curator for his father in Asker. On 25 January 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1862 he was named minister to Renneso, on 12 February 1870 he moved to Flekkefjord 
2 CONT
2 CONT and finally on 26 July 1880 he was named minister to Tvedt where he suddenly died 
2 CONT
2 CONT (from a heart stroke) on 25 January 1882.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married in Enebak on 28 December 1852 to Anne Hermine Steenbuch, born in Haaland
2 CONT
2 CONT on 29 May 1827, died suddenly by an accident on 23 October 1901. She was the oldest
2 CONT
2 CONT daughter of minister Hans Steenbuch who later moved to Enebak, (born 1802, died 1853) 
2 CONT
2 CONT and Karen Jensine Henny, 10 children. (No. 154-163)
