1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gustav Conrad Hansen (1831-1910) was one of Tønsberg's prominent businessmen in the 1800s. He was born in Tønsberg in 1831, the son of a merchant and mayor Hans Hansen and Caroline Mathilde f. Lyngaas. As a 25-year
2 CONC -old, he started his own merchant business and ran the shipping company next door. Hansen was among the world's first tanker shipowners when he in 1877 built on three of its sailing ships to be able to carry oil in bulk rather tha
2 CONC n in barrels. He evolved to become one of its most successful shipowners and attended beside the municipal life. For a period, he was deputy mayor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gustav Conrad Hansen is buried at Vestre Cemetery in Oslo. Title Shipowner used on the headstone. Gustav Hansen street in his hometown Tønsberg is named after him.
2 CONT
2 CONT TRANSLATED FROM NORWEGIAN: http://www.vestfoldarkivet.no/fru-gustav-conrad-hansen/
