1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1801 census for Kristiansand:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.digitalarkivet.no/en/census/person/pf01058333003741
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.naha.stolaf.edu/pubs/nas/volume12/vol12_4.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT The Reymert family dates back to the Gothic invasion of Spain, whence the name originated. They settled first in Holstein, and then in Norway over five hundred years ago (about 1372 A.D.). Father, son, grandson, and great-grandson
2 CONC  were in succession the pastors of the same church at Søgue Parish from 1636 to 1738. The mother, Jessie Sinclair Denoon, was a Scotch lady of the Campbell clan, whose family grounds were a part of the present Argyle estate near t
2 CONC he Clyde, where the castle of Denoon yet stands. Two uncles fought in the American Revolution; one died in the naval service. An uncle on the mother's side was in disfavor with the British because in his publication he favored the
2 CONC  independence of the American colonies. He came to the United States during the Revolution. He preached for fifty years in the "Auld Stane Kirk" at Caledonia, New York. The name of the Reverend Alexander Denoon is yet venerated by
2 CONC  the Scotch there.
