1 OCCU Referred to as Fyrst or Prince.  Bank Director, ship builder and fleet owner, Member of parliament, founder of Hans Johnsen firma. Knighted by Danish king. Hereditary Prince de Andreville., stadshauptmann og bankadministrator
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Comment by Erik Meldal-Johnsen :  '''In Wiki article : '''http://nn.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johan_Christian_Johnsen''' , Hans Johnsen referred to " Fyrst"  which translated in English means "Prince". Using the wiki tran
2 CONC slator and Google translate it says the following:''' Johan Christian Johnsen ( July 23, 1815 - February 2, 1898 ) was a Norwegian journalist , editor , member of parliament for the party Left and lexicographer . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Johnsen was from Kristiansand , where his father was superintendent in poor relief.  Although he was in his youth employed in his '''uncle Prince Hans Johnsen'''  trading business, so his stepfather T. O Fuglli say similar busines
2 CONC s.  He then traveled to the sea, but after a few trips he gave up sailor life.  Furthermore, he worked at a lumber office in 1834 before he was employed at a trading office in Antwerp .  Coming home to Norway he was an agent in OP
2 CONC  Moe & Sun. In 1837, he went to  Stavanger . 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''HANS JOHNSEN BIOGRAPHY :'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Nykobing Falster in Denmark,  his father Johannes started a company there. Hans moved to Kristiansand, Norway in 1820 and on 9th June 1825 formed the firm "Hans Johnsen".
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans was chairman of the Kritiansand Chamber of Commerce from 1848 until 1850 and also was elected "stadshauptman"  of the town. He was also appointed to the board of the Norges Bank and served as a director from 1846 until 1872. 
2 CONC He served as  a member of parliament for Kristiansand as well.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Johnsen was inducted as a ridder (knight) into the Order of Dannebrog. (Ridder Dannebrog Order - RDO)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Added 2nd April 2013:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Johnsen (2 August 1800-5. April 1872) was a Danish-Norwegian merchant and Member of Parliament. He was the father Jørgen Johnsen, while Johan Christian Johnsen was a nephew.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johnsen was born in Nykøbing in Denmark. He immigrated to Kristiansand and Norway in 1820, and became a merchant in the city in 1825. Year 1840 he was a civil Captain, 1852 mayor. From 1857 he was president (chairman) of the gas p
2 CONC lant in Kristiansand.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johnsen was for many years a member of the City Council. In 1845 he was elected to represent the town in Parliament. He was then a member of the Protocol Committee.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in Kristiansand  in 1872.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source : Lindstøl, Tallak: Parliament and Minister 1814-1914. Christiania, 1914
2 CONT
2 CONT '''http://nn.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hans_Johnsen'''
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT From Norwegian Wiki   '''http://nn.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johan_Christian_Johnsen'''   on Johan Christian Johnsen ( nephew of Hans Johnsen) translated by Google translate. Interesting that the google translation calls Hans Prince Hans
2 CONC  Johnsen from Norwegian "Fyrst" which is same as German Furst.
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian Johnsen (23 July 1815-2. February 1898) was a Norwegian journalist, editor, Member of Parliament for the Liberal Party, and lexicographer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johnsen was from Kristiansand, where his father was superintendent in poor relief. Although he was in his youth employed in his '''uncle Prince Hans Johnsen''' say trading business, so his stepfather T. O Fuglli say similar busine
2 CONC ss. He then traveled to the sea, but after a few trips he gave up sailor life. Furthermore, he worked at a lumber office in 1834 before he was employed at a trading office in Antwerp. Coming home to Norway he was an agent in OP Mo
2 CONC e & Sun, year 1837, he took himself to the acumen of Stavanger.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johnson was editor of Stavanger Amtstidende 1843-46, and edited monthly publication for young people who came out in Stavanger in 1846-47. He founded in 1848 the magazine Almuevennen week and ran the printing of Christiania, who p
2 CONC rinted this newspaper and various writings and books. From 1855 came the voucher Address magazine, with more political fabric than Almuevennen. He sold the magazine Almuevennen Fatherland in 1893, a magazine under the name Land bl
2 CONC ade went in in 1911. These supplementary sheet measures he tried to get out a new television, both in 1866 and 1870.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johnsen Stavanger represented by the Parliament in 1848, 1851 and 1854. He was in 1848 secretary of the industry committee No. 2, on the other two large Inga he was a member of the Customs Committee. From 1845 to 1851 he was a mem
2 CONC ber of Stavanger city council. He was the first chairman of 'The Norwegian holding company'.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johnson moved to Christiania after he was elected to the state auditor in 1854. This position he had to 1878, he said, when given off.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johnsen's trebandsverk Norwegian Haandlexikon for charitable Kundskaber came out in the period 1879 to 1888. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wiki on Hans. '''http://nn.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hans_Johnsen'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Johnsen (2. august 1800–5. april 1872) var ein dansk-norsk kjøpmann og stortingsmann. Han var far til Jørgen Johnsen, medan Johan Christian Johnsen var ein brorson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johnsen var fødd i Nykøbing i Danmark. Han innvandra til Kristiansand og Noreg i 1820, og vart kjøpmann i byen i 1825. År 1840 var han borgarkaptein, 1852 stadshauptmann. Frå 1857 var han direktør (styreleiar) for gassverket i Kri
2 CONC stiansand.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johnsen var mangeårig medlem av Kristiansand bystyre. I 1845 vart han vald å representere byen på Stortinget. Han var då medlem av protokollkomiteen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Han døydde i Kristiansand i 1872.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Kjelde [endre]Lindstøl, Tallak:Stortinget og Statsraadet 1814-1914. Kristiania, 1914
