1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Added by Erik Meldal-Johnsen 16/7/2026.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Frantz Oscar Johnsen (born in Kristiansand 4 July 1838, died in Sarpsborg 10 September 1905) was a doctor and politician. He was a representative and deputy representative for Sarpsborg in Parliament, mayor of the same city
2 CONC  and company doctor for several large companies in the area.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Background and family:
2 CONT His parents were merchant, mayor and member of parliament Hans Johnsen (1800-1872) and his wife Charlotte Amalie Loss (1806-1879). Like his father, his brother Jørgen and also his cousin Johan Christian Johnsen, he was also a memb
2 CONC er of the parliament.
2 CONT Joseph Johnsen was married twice. The first marriage, on 30 July 1868, was with Elisabeth Methea Kirstina Høy (1843-1870), who was the daughter of bank manager in Stavanger Andreas Høy and his wife Kirstine Elisabeth Kirsebom. As 
2 CONC a widower, Johnsen remarried in Kristiania on 15 October 1874 to Karoline Mathilde Mohr (b. 1854), who was the daughter of sanitary director Nils Georg Mohr and Kristine Hjersing.
2 CONT Joseph Johnsen had two daughters from the second marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Education and professional career:
2 CONT Joseph Johnsen became a student in 1858, privately taught by "Candidatus magisterii" Schnitzel. Johnsen took the "examen philosophicum" in 1866 and was graduated in the same year as a "Candidatus magisterii". He was appointed as a
2 CONC  candidate at Rikshospitalet's main department. Then, from 1869, he came to Sarpsborg as a practitioner for the large companies Hafslund, Borregaard and Solli bruk (in Tune). From 1870 he was also a railway doctor. For a short per
2 CONC iod he was appointed as a district doctor. He was on study trips in Berlin and Vienna in 1870-1871, and again in Vienna in 1883.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Politician:
2 CONT Johnsen and his family remained permanently in Sarpsborg, and he became involved in the town's public life. He was a member of the city council from 1880, and mayor of the city in 1889-1892. He was a deputy representative to the p
2 CONC arliament in 1889-1891, representative in 1892-1894 and again deputy in 1895-1897 and 1898-1900. During the time in the parliament, 1892-1894, he had a seat at the constitutional committee. In 1895, he joined the gas and pension c
2 CONC ommittee.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Literature:
2 CONT Lindstøl, Tallak: Stortinget og statsraadet 1814-1914, bd. 1. Kristiania 1914.
2 CONT Studenterne fra 1858. Biografiske meddelelser samlede ved Joh. K. Bergwitz. Kristiania 1908.
2 CONT Oscar Johnsen i Historisk befolkningsregister
2 CONT
2 CONT (Source: https://lokalhistoriewiki.no/wiki/Joseph_Frantz_Oscar_Johnsen )
