1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/64529331/brynjolf-hovde
2 CONT ----<br/>
2 CONT '''The following overview of Brynjolf Kolbeinson Hovde's family is taken from his autobiography, titled One Thing and Another from the Life of Pastor B. Hovde, which is dated July, 1916 at Neenah, Wisconsin.'''<br/>
2 CONT <br/>'''ABOUT MY FAMILY'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT My father's father, Johannes K. Hovde, died before I was born, whereas my  father's mother, Britha Liland Hovde, in my childhood was bedridden after a heart attack.  She was born in 1777, married 1794 at the age of 17. My mother's
2 CONC  father was Wilhelm  Berge (in the Voss dialect Villlum, in English William). He was a brother of the grandfather  of Prof. Knut and Pastor John Bergh, who were my second cousins. I do not know the  birth date of my mother's mothe
2 CONC r. My grandparents on mother's side were dead before my  time. My mother, Sigvord W., b.1798, d.10/12, 1882, was their only child.
2 CONT
2 CONT My grandparents on father's side (Johannes and Britha Hovde) had 10 children, 6  sons and 4 daughters. '''My father, Kolbein Johannessen Hovde was the oldest, b.1795,  d.1878.'''<br/>
2 CONT The '''others''' were: Johannes, '''Brynjolf''', Ole (Mandal), Ole (Hovde), Torstein, Anna,  Gjwerrud, Britha and Marthe. As the oldest my father stayed with the farm. <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Uncle '''Brynjolf''' (Bryngel) married Mari G. Saeve and bought a part of the farm Berge. By an earlier marriage Mari had a son Mathis and a daughter Britha. With Uncle Brynjolf she had 4 sons and 2 daughters: Johannes, Anved, Bry
2 CONC njolf, Nils, Britha and Martha. Anved was a peddler in other counties, whereas Johannes and Brynjolf emigrated to America to Liberty Prairie, Wis. Here Johannes settled as a farmer and married Augunna Mikkelsdtr. Erdal, a sister o
2 CONC f our Past. Gullik Erdal. Brynjolf lived at their farm. In 1857 even the old parents came over and with them Britha, Nils and Martha. Britha was married to Nikolai G. Erdal, a brother of Past. Erdal. The youngest son, Nils, was ap
2 CONC pointed pastor in the synod and died 1883 in New Hope, Wis. His wife was Miss Kittelsen. They had 2 sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
