1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The known history of the Reymert family goes back to the brothers Henrik Marcussen Reimer (1633-1713) and Christen Marcussen Reimer (1636-1699). Both of them probably came To Norway from Køge in Denmark. They were 
2 CONC both pastors in Søgne parish in Vest-Agder in Norway. (The t- ending probably came in use during the 18th century.) (Source: «Familien Reymert i Mandal» by Øivind T. Reymert, Lørenskog 1990.)
2 CONT
2 CONT The mother, Jessie Sinclair Denoon, was a Scotch lady of the Campbell clan, whose family grounds were a part of the present Argyle estate near the Clyde, where the castle of Denoon yet stands. Two uncles fought in the American Rev
2 CONC olution; one died in the naval service. An uncle on the mother's side was in disfavor with the British because in his publication he favored the independence of the American colonies. He came to the United States during the Revolu
2 CONC tion. He preached for fifty years in the "Auld Stane Kirk" at Caledonia, New York. The name of the Reverend Alexander Denoon is yet venerated by the Scotch there.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.naha.stolaf.edu/pubs/nas/volume12/vol12_4.htm
