1 OCCU Agriculturalist
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gabriel was born to a wealthy merchant family living in Bragernes, Drammen, Norway.  He was educated to become an agriculturalist. In 1847 Gabriel was visiting with his brother-in-law, John Collett, when Gabriel ha
2 CONC d a romance with a local farm girl. The romance produced a son, Sebjørn Gabrielsen Smith, who later emigrated to America. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In about 1857, Gabriel's father, Elias, turned over the management of the Hotel North to Gabriel, along with Gabriel's brother-in-law. In 1865, Gabriel was living in a large apartment with a widow, Eleonore Johanne Bergh, and was 
2 CONC unmarried. He was working as an administrator. Four years later he married Maren Sofie Schive, a union that produced nine children, six of whom grew to adulthood. At the same time as his marriage, he became the first manager of th
2 CONC e agricultural institute "Kauffeldske" at the farm Overby in Vardal. In 1883, he became an agriculturalist with Toftes Gave at Helgoen. From 1885 - 1893, he was overseer of Øvre Ekers in Sjøl. In 1893, he retired and moved to Oslo
2 CONC . He died there at the age of 84.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Drammensfamilien Smith, Genealogiske og Personalhistoriske Oplysninger ved A. Iuel, 1934.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gabriel Benjamin Smith'''
2 CONT
