2 CONT The last name of Theodora’s great-great-grandfather was Hansen (see below under Hans Nicolai Cormontan).  He lived for a time in Hjertesberg i Stege, Denmark.  Hjertesberg is a small hamlet about 3-4 miles from Stege, the largest 
2 CONC town on the island of Møe in southeastern Denmark.  Hansen changed his patronymic last name to take the name of the place where he lived.  Additionally, he utilized the Latin equivalent of Hjertesberg, which is Cor montan. The two
2 CONC  words translate as “Heart of the Mountain.”
